  "paragraph": 8,
  "text": "During prefill, the GPU loads each layer's weights from HBM once and multiplies them against a huge matrix of hundreds or thousands of input tokens together. That matrix-matrix multiply, called GEMM, keeps Tensor Cores packed with work. It is like a freight train hauling a thousand containers in one trip.",
